  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A hollow metal sphere of radius $R$ is charged with a charge $Q .$ The electric potential and intensity inside the sphere are respectively",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "WOTj7",
      "text": "$\\frac{Q}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_{0} R^{2}}$ and $\\frac{Q}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_{0} R}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dVJSQ",
      "text": "$\\frac{Q}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_{0} R}$ and zero",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yGbr8",
      "text": "zero and zero",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TjnVi",
      "text": "$\\frac{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_{0} Q}{R}$ and $\\frac{Q}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_{0} R^{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Inside a hollow charged sphere, the electric field intensity is always zero.\r\n$\\therefore$ $E=0$ but potential is constant.\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2016_phy_a3.png\">\r\nPotential on the surtace of the hollow sphere\r\n$$\r\nV=\\frac{K Q}{R}=\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_{0}} \\cdot \\frac{Q}{R}=\\frac{Q}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_{0} R}\r\n$$\r\nThis is the potential $(\\mathrm{V})$ inside the charged hollow meta sphere.",
    "image": null
  },
